<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96924" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοιχάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοῖχος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in a row one behind another</i>, esp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ Στοιχάδες</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσοι</span>), name of the islands which lie
				<i>in a row</i> east of Toulon, now <i>les Îles d'
				Hyères</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.554
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλᾶαι ς</span>. olive-trees (prob.
			because planted <i>in rows</i>) which were not sacred,
			like the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορίαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Sol.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				62
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοιχάς, ἡ</span>, an aromatic plant, <i>cassidony, Lavandula
				Stoechas</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				918
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
